  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 327 AM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nThe upper pattern translates slowly east Sunday into next week with \nthe upper level ridge moving across the Midwest into the Great Lakes \nRegion by midweek.  Meanwhile, the surface high drifts southeast \ninto the Ohio Valley by Monday, and then continues into the Mid \nAtlantic Region by Wednesday and Thursday.  Temperatures across the \nMid Mississippi Valley will slowly warm back to near seasonal \nnormals in the mid 50s by Tuesday/Wednesday according to the NBM. \nThis is backed up by the LREF, which is showing very similar \ntemperatures through the period.  The interquartile range of \ntemperatures in the ensembles is also very tight through midweek, 2-\n3 degrees through Tuesday, and only 3-5 degrees on Wednesday and \nThursday. This lends a high degree of confidence to the forecast \nthrough the period.  There won't be any chance for precip under the \ninfluence of the surface high and upper level ridge through \nWednesday.  However, global deterministic guidance shows a short \nwave trough moving through the Great Plains late Wednesday and into \nthe upper Midwest on Thursday.  The low level reflection of the \ntrough pushes another cold front into the Midwest with some modest \nlow level moisture return ahead of it.  The NBM paints 20-30 PoPs \nover much of the area Thursday, and around 30% of the LREF members \nhave precip for our area as well, so the NBM's PoPs seem reasonable.",
